---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { LAST_UPDATED, AUTHOR_NAME, CONTACT_EMAIL, AUTHOR_ROLE, SITE_NAMES } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
import { organizationSchema, breadcrumbSchema, profilePageSchema } from '../../lib/seo';
import { displayDate } from '../../lib/format';
import { PAGES } from '../../lib/guides';
const lang = 'en';
const n = PAGES.length + 1;
---
<PageLayout title="Radif Partners, publisher of Medical Coding Cost: who we are" description="Who publishes Medical Coding Cost, where its exam, membership and renewal fees come from, how they are dated and checked, and what the site will never sell you." lang={lang} jsonLd={[organizationSchema(lang), profilePageSchema({ path: route('about', lang), lang }), breadcrumbSchema([{ name: 'Home', path: route('home', lang) }, { name: 'About', path: route('about', lang) }])]} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'About' }]}>
  <header class="mb-6"><p class="mb-1 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-accent-600">About</p><h1 class="mt-0 text-3xl font-bold text-navy-900 md:text-4xl">Who is behind {SITE_NAMES[lang]}</h1></header>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <div class="not-prose mb-6"><p class="text-lg font-semibold text-navy-900">{AUTHOR_NAME}</p><p class="text-navy-700">{AUTHOR_ROLE[lang]}</p></div>
    <p>{SITE_NAMES[lang]} is published by {AUTHOR_NAME}, a company that turns public fee schedules and public data into free calculators. This site is for people deciding whether to become a medical coder or biller, for coders choosing a second credential, and for anyone who has seen three different prices for the same exam on three school websites.</p>
    <h2>What you will find here</h2>
    <p>The exam, membership and renewal fees of the AAPC credentials (CPC, COC, CIC, CRC, CPB) and of the AHIMA coding credentials (CCA, CCS, CCS-P), set side by side; the format of each exam we could read; the first-time pass rates AHIMA publishes and the retakes they imply; the CEUs and fees that keep a credential active; the dates of an AAPC exam path; and the count of coding certificates and degrees awarded in each state in the federal IPEDS file. Every page has a calculator, and none asks for an email address.</p>
    <h2>Where the figures come from</h2>
    <p>Fees and rules were read on the AAPC and AHIMA pages named on each page, with the date of reading. AHIMA's terms ask for written approval before linking to its inner pages, so AHIMA figures name the page they come from and link to AHIMA's home page. The <a href={route('method', lang)}>method page</a> explains each calculation.</p>
    <h2>What we are not</h2>
    <p>We are not AAPC, AHIMA, NHA, a test vendor, a school or an employer. We cannot sell a voucher, book an exam or check your eligibility. We publish no salary figure and no ranking of schools, and nothing on the site is medical content: it is about fees, formats and deadlines.</p>
    <h2>How the site is funded</h2>
    <p>Nothing is sold here: no course, no study guide, no referral fee from a school. If advertising appears one day, it will stay out of the calculators, which never see what you type.</p>
    <h2>Report a mistake</h2>
    <p>Write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> with the fee and the page where you saw a different one. The <a href={route('editorial', lang)}>editorial policy</a> says how corrections are made and dated. The site has {n} pages.</p>
    <p class="text-sm text-navy-600">Fees last checked on <time datetime={LAST_UPDATED}>{displayDate(LAST_UPDATED, 'en-US')}</time>.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
